{
  "id": "grammar.a1.cafe.03.querer",
  "title": "Querer",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Say what you would like",
      "content": "You've already met querer (to want) for saying what you want. Here's a quick recap, now put to use in a *café*: order with quiero + what you'd like."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Querer in the present (recap)",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "quiero"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "quieres"
        ],
        [
          "él / ella / usted",
          "quiere"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros / nosotras",
          "queremos"
        ],
        [
          "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
          "quieren"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Quiero un café.",
          "english": "I would like a coffee."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Qué quieres?",
          "english": "What would you like?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Ella quiere un té.",
          "english": "She would like a tea."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Queremos dos sándwiches.",
          "english": "We would like two sandwiches."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "In a *café*, quiero + food or drink is a simple and natural way to make an order."
    }
  ]
}
